Each term is the sum of the three before it, starting from 0, -1, -1. Since the sequence can go negative, this uses signed `long long`:

```cpp
#include <iostream>

// Returns the nth term of the sequence, where
// T(0) = 0, T(1) = -1, T(2) = -1, and T(n) = T(n-1) + T(n-2) + T(n-3).
long long sequence(unsigned int n) {
    if (n == 0) {
        return 0;
    }
    if (n == 1 || n == 2) {
        return -1;
    }
    return sequence(n - 1) + sequence(n - 2) + sequence(n - 3);
}

