Standard approach: for each cell that is `*`, treat it as a possible tick center. Compute the maximum d such that cells (i-h, j±h) are all `*` for h = 1..d. If d ≥ k, mark all of those cells as covered (for h = 0..d). Finally, every `*` must be covered.

Using the maximal d for each center is optimal, since a larger tick only covers more cells and all of them are black.

