If the total sum is composite, take everything. Otherwise the sum is prime. Since n ≥ 3 and the elements are distinct, the sum is at least 6, so a prime sum must be odd (the only even prime is 2). That means at least one element is odd. Removing a single odd element makes the sum even. The remaining sum is at least 2 + ... and is greater than 2 because n ≥ 3 and the elements are distinct and positive (the remaining two elements sum to at least 3, and an even sum ≥ 3 is ≥ 4), so it is composite.

```python
import sys
